 This file contains technical details, architectural decisions, and important implementation notes for future development sessions.
 
+## Branch: `heroku-deploy` (single-dyno deployment)
+
+This branch adapts the local-only app for a **monolithic single-dyno Heroku deployment**. The `master` branch keeps the original local two-process setup.
+
+**What changed:**
+- **Monolithic architecture:** FastAPI now serves both the `/api/*` routes AND the pre-built React frontend (`frontend/dist/`) via `StaticFiles` + an SPA catch-all. One `web` process only.
+- **`$PORT`:** `backend/main.py` reads `PORT` from env (`int(os.getenv("PORT", 8001))`).
+- **Route order is critical:** all `/api/*` routes are declared BEFORE the `/{full_path:path}` SPA catch-all (FastAPI resolves in declaration order). The catch-all also guards with `if full_path.startswith("api")`. The old `GET /` health check moved to `GET /api/health` so `/` serves `index.html`.
+- **CORS:** dynamic origins — localhost (dev) + `https://$HEROKU_APP_NAME.herokuapp.com` + optional `$CUSTOM_DOMAIN`.
+- **Configurable models:** `COUNCIL_MODELS` (comma-separated) and `CHAIRMAN_MODEL` read from env, with defaults. Reconfigurable via `heroku config:set` without redeploy.
+- **Storage path:** `DATA_DIR` env-configurable. Filesystem is ephemeral on Heroku (TODO: migrate to Heroku Postgres).
+- **Frontend API base:** `frontend/src/api.js` uses relative paths in prod (`import.meta.env.PROD`), `http://localhost:8001` in dev; overridable via `VITE_API_URL`. Vite has a `/api` dev proxy.
+- **Two buildpacks (order matters):** `heroku/nodejs` (builds frontend via root `package.json` `heroku-postbuild`) then `heroku/python` (installs `requirements.txt`, runs `Procfile`).
+
+**Files added at root:** `Procfile`, `runtime.txt`, `requirements.txt`, `app.json`, `package.json` (delegating build), `.env.example`.
+
+**Branding (AfricAIsoft):** page title `LLM Council — AfricAIsoft`, discreet `Powered by AfricAIsoft` footer, accent color `#1a5276`.
+
 ## Project Overview
 
 LLM Council is a 3-stage deliberation system where multiple LLMs collaboratively answer user questions. The key innovation is anonymized peer review in Stage 2, preventing models from playing favorites.
